Yes. You have to scoop the eels out with that net.

1032
00:43:42,870 --> 00:43:45,370
(Each eel weighs 1kg on average.)

1033
00:43:45,910 --> 00:43:47,956
(About 4,000 eels they caught multiplied by 1kg equals...)

1034
00:43:47,980 --> 00:43:50,080
(About 4t!)

1035
00:43:50,750 --> 00:43:52,049
(They have to scoop out 4t of eels in total with a net!)

1036
00:43:52,050 --> 00:43:53,050
It must be really exhausting.

1037
00:43:53,051 --> 00:43:54,626
(They have to scoop out 4t of eels in total with a net!)

1038
00:43:54,650 --> 00:43:55,720
I'll give it a try.

1039
00:43:57,350 --> 00:44:00,160
(The eel fanatic learns how to use the net.)

1040
00:44:00,290 --> 00:44:01,420
(Going in)

1041
00:44:01,620 --> 00:44:04,390
(Step 1: Push the net as deep as possible.)

1042
00:44:04,930 --> 00:44:07,600
All the way to the wall? Because if we don't, they will escape?

1043
00:44:08,760 --> 00:44:11,430
(An eel fountain explodes.)

1044
00:44:11,830 --> 00:44:14,170
(Passing the net)

1045
00:44:15,040 --> 00:44:16,769
(It looks heavy at a glance.)

1046
00:44:16,770 --> 00:44:17,840
What?

1047
00:44:18,140 --> 00:44:20,410
(Shocked)

1048
00:44:21,840 --> 00:44:24,579
(The eels that were moved into the bucket...)

1049
00:44:24,580 --> 00:44:25,619
One, two, three.

1050
00:44:25,620 --> 00:44:27,980
(should be transferred straight into the water tanks!)

1051
00:44:28,520 --> 00:44:31,290
(They work in pairs so they don't lose the precious eels.)

1052
00:44:31,720 --> 00:44:34,390
(Delivering the eels to the waiting water tank)

1053
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:36,930
(The first delivery is complete.)

1054
00:44:41,160 --> 00:44:42,429
Pushing it into the water like this...

1055
00:44:42,430 --> 00:44:46,040
(Now, they have to move about 4,267kg of eels.)

1056
00:44:46,570 --> 00:44:49,370
(The eel fanatic tries to use the net as she learned.)

1057
00:44:49,840 --> 00:44:52,170
(She pushes the net as deep as it goes.)

1058
00:44:52,640 --> 00:44:54,580
(Then she pushes it toward the wall.)

1059
00:44:54,880 --> 00:44:57,200
(After driving enough eels into the net, she lifts it up.)

1060
00:44:58,280 --> 00:44:59,380
Here we go.

1061
00:45:00,220 --> 00:45:03,350
(She can feel the eels' power through her hands.)

1062
00:45:04,250 --> 00:45:06,690
(Looks like she got a massive scoop of eels.)

1063
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:09,129
(Lifting)

1064
00:45:09,130 --> 00:45:10,160
Hold there.

1065
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:13,480
(Sun Young scooped out more eels than the eel farm owner.)

1066
00:45:13,900 --> 00:45:15,580
My goodness. She scooped out so many eels.

1067
00:45:20,740 --> 00:45:23,140
(Even the eel farm worker is surprised by the sheer volume.)

1068
00:45:23,240 --> 00:45:25,169
(I'm good at this, right?)

1069
00:45:25,170 --> 00:45:27,370
So, you don't catch the eels with your bare hands here.

1070
00:45:27,640 --> 00:45:29,079
Catching them with your bare hands is more fun.

1071
00:45:29,080 --> 00:45:31,026
(Sun Young is disappointed that she can't catch them barehanded.)

1072
00:45:31,050 --> 00:45:33,650
(So she scoops eels out.)

1073
00:45:34,950 --> 00:45:37,450
(She scoops out more eels.)

1074
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:40,490
(Even when she's surrounded by a school of eels...)

1075
00:45:40,790 --> 00:45:42,689
Let's go! That's good!

1076
00:45:42,690 --> 00:45:44,530
(She shows no hesitation.)

1077
00:45:45,190 --> 00:45:48,500
(She doesn't mind getting soaked. She might just dive into the water.)

1078
00:45:48,560 --> 00:45:49,629
Okay.

1079
00:45:49,630 --> 00:45:52,440
(She keeps scooping eels to make up for not using her bare hands.)

1080
00:45:52,640 --> 00:45:53,800
(Run!)

1081
00:45:54,140 --> 00:45:55,199
That's what I'm talking about.

1082
00:45:55,200 --> 00:45:57,670
(She's a disaster for the eels.)

1083
00:45:58,540 --> 00:45:59,979
(Chuckling)

1084
00:45:59,980 --> 00:46:01,880
(You brats)

1085
00:46:03,150 --> 00:46:06,449
(Do not run away, eels.)

1086
00:46:06,450 --> 00:46:09,850
(You'll end up in my net anyway.)

1087
00:46:10,320 --> 00:46:11,890
Sun Young, you're so cool.

1088
00:46:13,060 --> 00:46:14,660
I could even take a bath in here.

1089
00:46:15,630 --> 00:46:17,129
(That's sheer madness.)

1090
00:46:17,130 --> 00:46:19,330
I want to catch them with my bare hands.

1091
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:23,170
But I can't do that in here.

1092
00:46:24,030 --> 00:46:26,600
(They're simply amazed.)

1093
00:46:26,700 --> 00:46:28,369
I see a whole bunch of eels here.

1094
00:46:28,370 --> 00:46:31,170
(While Sun Young, the eel fanatic, is riding a crazy dopamine rush...)

1095
00:46:31,410 --> 00:46:33,286
We can do it faster if we do it in pairs, right?

1096
00:46:33,310 --> 00:46:35,256
- You mean, scooping them out?
- Yes, I'll help her...

1097
00:46:35,280 --> 00:46:37,149
scoop them out in the fish holder.

1098
00:46:37,150 --> 00:46:38,710
(Jin Hee decided to go into the water.)

1099
00:46:38,880 --> 00:46:42,180
(He starts scooping eels out!)

1100
00:46:43,520 --> 00:46:46,190
(Jin Hee pushes the net as if he were scraping the bottom.)

1101
00:46:46,860 --> 00:46:49,560
(Skillful)

1102
00:46:50,060 --> 00:46:51,259
(He got a massive scoop in one go.)

1103
00:46:51,260 --> 00:46:52,530
Oh, my. That's a lot.

1104
00:46:55,060 --> 00:46:56,800
Jin Hee, you're so good at this...

1105
00:46:57,070 --> 00:46:58,830
- He's good. He's strong too.
- Indeed.

1106
00:46:59,500 --> 00:47:00,999
- What would we do without him?
- Exactly.

1107
00:47:01,000 --> 00:47:02,920
(Seriously, what would they do without Jin Hee?)

1108
00:47:03,640 --> 00:47:06,310
(Everyone raves about Jin Hee, who's doing a great job.)

1109
00:47:07,480 --> 00:47:10,849
(Jin Hee, until you came...)

1110
00:47:10,850 --> 00:47:14,679
(I've never been caught.)

1111
00:47:14,680 --> 00:47:17,889
(Jin Hee, you have no idea...)

1112
00:47:17,890 --> 00:47:21,890
(that there's no one else who does better than you.)

1113
00:47:22,430 --> 00:47:25,290
(He's good at this.)

1114
00:47:25,800 --> 00:47:29,270
(Next to Jin Hee, who's working hard and quietly...)

1115
00:47:29,400 --> 00:47:30,400
(Laughing)

1116
00:47:31,430 --> 00:47:35,370
Oh, my. This is no joke. It's so satisfying.

1117
00:47:35,840 --> 00:47:37,869
- Here we go.
- Come on in, you brats.

1118
00:47:37,870 --> 00:47:39,309
All right. Here we go.

1119
00:47:39,310 --> 00:47:42,080
(The mad net duo)

1120
00:47:42,380 --> 00:47:43,849
How about we work as a team?

1121
00:47:43,850 --> 00:47:45,410
- Okay.
- Good.

1122
00:47:45,780 --> 00:47:46,849
Push it down into the water.

1123
00:47:46,850 --> 00:47:47,850
(They push their nets down into the water first!)

1124
00:47:47,851 --> 00:47:50,549
- Push it down. Two, three.
- One, two, three. Let's go.

1125
00:47:50,550 --> 00:47:53,090
(Jin Hee's plan is to drive the eels in the same direction!)

1126
00:47:53,560 --> 00:47:54,660
(Grunting)

1127
00:47:57,160 --> 00:48:00,400
(Their teamwork brought a great result.)

1128
00:48:00,530 --> 00:48:02,236
But when will we finish scooping out all these eels?

1129
00:48:02,260 --> 00:48:03,770
There are 4,000 eels in here.

1130
00:48:05,570 --> 00:48:08,069
- Yes. That's good.
- Oh, gosh.

1131
00:48:08,070 --> 00:48:09,439
(A replacement appears.)

1132
00:48:09,440 --> 00:48:10,740
Oh, my. This is amazing.

1133
00:48:11,710 --> 00:48:12,710
(While You Seok is amazed by the first-time sensation...)

1134
00:48:12,711 --> 00:48:13,810
See?

1135
00:48:14,310 --> 00:48:16,410
(Yoon Seo joins them.)

1136
00:48:16,710 --> 00:48:19,180
(Jin Hee is in charge of moving the eels.)

1137
00:48:19,220 --> 00:48:20,279
Be careful.

1138
00:48:20,280 --> 00:48:21,450
(Be careful, Jin Hee.)

1139
00:48:21,880 --> 00:48:22,949
(Passing the bucket)

1140
00:48:22,950 --> 00:48:24,519
- I was told to go this way.
- I'll show you how it's done.

1141
00:48:24,520 --> 00:48:25,959
- Let's drive them together.
- I learned how to do this.

1142
00:48:25,960 --> 00:48:28,290
- Push it down and step forward.
- Yes.

1143
00:48:28,720 --> 00:48:29,890
When it hits the wall,

1144
00:48:30,130 --> 00:48:31,559
(Drive them.)

1145
00:48:31,560 --> 00:48:33,000
- lift it up. Oh, gosh.
- Gosh.

1146
00:48:34,300 --> 00:48:36,969
(The younger members who are still energetic...)

1147
00:48:36,970 --> 00:48:38,000
It's so heavy.

1148
00:48:38,400 --> 00:48:41,140
(They drive the eels with their youthful energy.)

1149
00:48:41,300 --> 00:48:42,640
Gosh, it's so heavy.

1150
00:48:47,240 --> 00:48:50,210
(In the cool water, they enjoy the thrilling sensation.)

1151
00:48:50,310 --> 00:48:51,910
We won't need to go to the valley today.

1152
00:48:52,210 --> 00:48:53,279
- We're having all the fun in here.
- This basically is...

1153
00:48:53,280 --> 00:48:54,440
This basically is the valley.

1154
00:48:55,080 --> 00:48:57,420
(No!)

1155
00:48:57,820 --> 00:48:59,189
Calm down.

1156
00:48:59,190 --> 00:49:01,819
Please calm down. Can you...

1157
00:49:01,820 --> 00:49:03,030
You caught too many eels.

1158
00:49:04,190 --> 00:49:05,229
I think I caught too many.

1159
00:49:05,230 --> 00:49:06,329
(Yoon Seo got a massive scoop that's as big as herself.)

1160
00:49:06,330 --> 00:49:08,260
This won't be easy.

1161
00:49:13,600 --> 00:49:17,370
(The eels caught by Yoon Seo are too heavy for even two men to lift.)

1162
00:49:17,570 --> 00:49:18,870
Oh, my. It's a lot.

1163
00:49:21,910 --> 00:49:26,350
(The younger members, who are still energetic, are doing a great job.)

1164
00:49:28,780 --> 00:49:29,920
Sun Young is winking.

1165
00:49:32,520 --> 00:49:34,720
(Is this a wink?)

1166
00:49:35,220 --> 00:49:36,980
(It's an unusual wink, but it cheers me up.)

1167
00:49:37,590 --> 00:49:39,430
(Winking)

1168
00:49:39,900 --> 00:49:42,900
(The siblings muster up more energy.)

1169
00:49:44,300 --> 00:49:45,329
I caught too many.

1170
00:49:45,330 --> 00:49:47,269
(Even when a ton of eels are caught, she lifts them up easily.)

1171
00:49:47,270 --> 00:49:48,750
There are eels absolutely everywhere.

1172
00:49:50,410 --> 00:49:53,040
(Scoop out all the eels surrounding you.)

1173
00:49:53,440 --> 00:49:54,510
It's no joke, right?

1174
00:49:55,710 --> 00:49:57,150
I am the wild eel.

1175
00:49:59,180 --> 00:50:00,180
Let's go.

1176
00:50:01,080 --> 00:50:02,989
One, two, three. It's too heavy for you. Leave it.

1177
00:50:02,990 --> 00:50:05,990
(Current progress: 3,400kg scooped out of 4,282kg)

1178
00:50:06,320 --> 00:50:09,230
(Meanwhile, the eel farm owner is doing something.)

1179
00:50:09,530 --> 00:50:10,730
Oh, he's gathering the eels.

1180
00:50:11,730 --> 00:50:14,530
(Since there aren't many eels left, he's tightening the fish holder.)

1181
00:50:15,130 --> 00:50:17,200
There are still a lot of eels in here.

1182
00:50:17,870 --> 00:50:20,770
(They start scooping eels up again to wrap it up quickly.)

1183
00:50:23,840 --> 00:50:24,840
It's broken.

1184
00:50:26,540 --> 00:50:27,680
It's broken?

1185
00:50:28,780 --> 00:50:30,410
Let's throw this out.

1186
00:50:30,710 --> 00:50:31,780
My goodness.

1187
00:50:32,780 --> 00:50:35,620
(The pole of Jin Hee's net snapped.)

1188
00:50:39,790 --> 00:50:42,959
(Jin Hee just uses the net part to keep going!)

1189
00:50:42,960 --> 00:50:44,090
Let's go.

1190
00:50:44,790 --> 00:50:47,330
(Watching Jin Hee's amazing ability to get the job done, )

1191
00:50:47,860 --> 00:50:49,500
(everyone is simply impressed.)

1192
00:50:50,170 --> 00:50:52,940
(Thanks to the amazing work done by Jin Hee, the great worker...)

1193
00:50:52,970 --> 00:50:55,270
- It's finally close to an end.
- One, two...

1194
00:50:55,500 --> 00:50:57,170
It's closing in more and more.

1195
00:50:58,240 --> 00:51:00,039
(They must be almost done.)

1196
00:51:00,040 --> 00:51:01,840
(The fish holder has been tightened so much.)

1197
00:51:02,110 --> 00:51:03,580
Jin Hee, aren't you tired?

1198
00:51:04,950 --> 00:51:06,080
I'm tired, but this is fun.

1199
00:51:06,320 --> 00:51:07,550
It's fun, indeed, but...

1200
00:51:08,950 --> 00:51:11,119
When was the last time I worked this hard...

1201
00:51:11,120 --> 00:51:13,401
I think it's been 30 years since I last worked this hard.

1202
00:51:14,220 --> 00:51:16,259
Did you perhaps appear on a show...

1203
00:51:16,260 --> 00:51:17,260
like "Experience the Scene of Life?"

1204
00:51:17,261 --> 00:51:19,159
I didn't even go on "Experience the Scene of Life."

1205
00:51:19,160 --> 00:51:20,200
Oh, you didn't?

1206
00:51:20,630 --> 00:51:22,110
No, I thought it'd be too exhausting.

1207
00:51:23,100 --> 00:51:26,200
(Jin Hee refused to go on the show, thinking it'd be too exhausting.)

1208
00:51:26,700 --> 00:51:28,939
You Seok, you said you wanted to go to the valley.

1209
00:51:28,940 --> 00:51:29,970
(Shaking his head)

1210
00:51:30,410 --> 00:51:31,740
You don't need to go there?

1211
00:51:32,270 --> 00:51:33,610
Valley, my foot.

1212
00:51:34,640 --> 00:51:36,150
"Valley, my foot."

1213
00:51:37,410 --> 00:51:39,420
(That's so funny.)

1214
00:51:39,880 --> 00:51:40,979
We're actually almost done.

1215
00:51:40,980 --> 00:51:42,690
(Touched)

1216
00:51:42,820 --> 00:51:43,920
This is unbelievable.

1217
00:51:44,450 --> 00:51:46,890
I think this is the hardest work we've ever done on the show.

1218
00:51:47,020 --> 00:51:49,020
(Even though it's hard work...)

1219
00:51:49,330 --> 00:51:50,890
Be careful. They might escape.

1220
00:51:51,890 --> 00:51:52,930
Oh, that's good.

1221
00:51:53,900 --> 00:51:57,270
(Crowding around, they move the eels to the bucket.)

1222
00:51:57,400 --> 00:51:59,069
(Let's see.)

1223
00:51:59,070 --> 00:52:00,640
Done! There's none left, right?

1224
00:52:01,400 --> 00:52:02,669
- All right!
- There's none left!

1225
00:52:02,670 --> 00:52:04,709
(The work is done.)

1226
00:52:04,710 --> 00:52:06,070
I wish I could just lie down here.

1227
00:52:06,680 --> 00:52:08,720
Good job, guys. How many eels did we catch earlier?

1228
00:52:09,550 --> 00:52:11,149
- We caught 8,000 eels.
- I don't even know.

1229
00:52:11,150 --> 00:52:12,209
No, we caught 9,000 eels.

1230
00:52:12,210 --> 00:52:13,619
- I'm so...
- How many eels were there?

1231
00:52:13,620 --> 00:52:15,180
(They did a great job.)

1232
00:52:16,050 --> 00:52:18,949
- Great job, everyone.
- Great job.

1233
00:52:18,950 --> 00:52:20,689
- I can't believe we pulled it off.
- Exactly.

1234
00:52:20,690 --> 00:52:22,770
(After finishing the legendary eel catching work...)

1235
00:52:24,030 --> 00:52:26,899
(She's completely spaced out.)

1236
00:52:26,900 --> 00:52:27,999
Do you know what's happening to me?

1237
00:52:28,000 --> 00:52:31,600
This is what a dopamine addict ends up looking like.

1238
00:52:31,770 --> 00:52:34,700
You jump in thinking it'd be fun, and you end up like this.

1239
00:52:35,240 --> 00:52:37,810
You were indeed high on dopamine earlier.

1240
00:52:38,010 --> 00:52:41,240
This is why you shouldn't chase a dopamine rush too much.

1241
00:52:41,940 --> 00:52:44,580
(Too much dopamine is the shortcut to ruining your everyday life.)

1242
00:52:44,610 --> 00:52:45,750
Have some snacks.

1243
00:52:46,020 --> 00:52:47,779
- Thank you.
- Thank you for your hard work.

1244
00:52:47,780 --> 00:52:49,589
- Thank you for your help.
- Don't mention it.

1245
00:52:49,590 --> 00:52:50,590
- Thank you.
- Oh, my.

1246
00:52:50,591 --> 00:52:51,690
- What are these?
- Oh, my.

1247
00:52:53,160 --> 00:52:55,119
Gwangyang is the green plum capital of Korea.

1248
00:52:55,120 --> 00:52:56,506
(The snack set of green plums, Gwangyang's specialty)

1249
00:52:56,530 --> 00:52:59,189
These are plum blossom bread, green plum cream cheese bread,

1250
00:52:59,190 --> 00:53:00,600
and green plum muffin.

1251
00:53:01,000 --> 00:53:03,429
And I made slushy for you...

1252
00:53:03,430 --> 00:53:05,230
with the green plum syrup that my mom made.

1253
00:53:05,870 --> 00:53:07,099
(I love it.)

1254
00:53:07,100 --> 00:53:08,299
It was really hot, wasn't it?

1255
00:53:08,300 --> 00:53:09,409
- Thanks.
- Please enjoy.

1256
00:53:09,410 --> 00:53:11,270
- Thank you. We'll enjoy it.
- Thank you.

1257
00:53:12,240 --> 00:53:13,940
It feels like we're on a battlefield.

1258
00:53:14,840 --> 00:53:16,479
(She agrees.)

1259
00:53:16,480 --> 00:53:17,810
It's as if we were refugees...

1260
00:53:17,910 --> 00:53:19,920
eating on the side of the road.

1261
00:53:20,450 --> 00:53:21,450
We're eating boiled eggs.

1262
00:53:21,451 --> 00:53:22,919
As if we were eating the food we carried in our bags.

1263
00:53:22,920 --> 00:53:24,596
(They start eating the snack, looking like refugees.)

1264
00:53:24,620 --> 00:53:27,459
(She drinks cool green plum syrup slushy first.)

1265
00:53:27,460 --> 00:53:29,390
- It's good.
- It's so delicious.

1266
00:53:29,890 --> 00:53:31,090
I love this green plum slushy.

1267
00:53:33,200 --> 00:53:34,999
(It feels even cooler and sweeter after the hard work.)

1268
00:53:35,000 --> 00:53:36,069
It's so cool.

1269
00:53:36,070 --> 00:53:37,929
Is this our lunch?

1270
00:53:37,930 --> 00:53:39,129
No, that's breakfast.

1271
00:53:39,130 --> 00:53:41,069
- What time is it now?
- What about lunch?

1272
00:53:41,070 --> 00:53:42,199
It's 9:17am now.

1273
00:53:42,200 --> 00:53:44,139
- It's only 9am now?
- Really?

1274
00:53:44,140 --> 00:53:45,969
It's 9am now?

1275
00:53:45,970 --> 00:53:47,079
(She can't believe it.)

1276
00:53:47,080 --> 00:53:48,510
We left at 5:30am.

1277
00:53:49,180 --> 00:53:50,809
Then what should we do now?

