- It really is.

2532
01:39:04,266 --> 01:39:06,576
- It's seriously amazing.
- It's really amazing.

2533
01:39:07,936 --> 01:39:10,906
(It's even fresher as they caught it from the sea.)

2534
01:39:11,706 --> 01:39:14,475
- Gosh, the eel is huge.
- It's wonderful.

2535
01:39:14,476 --> 01:39:15,476
It really is wonderful.

2536
01:39:15,477 --> 01:39:16,515
(Plump and appetizing)

2537
01:39:16,516 --> 01:39:17,545
Gosh, this is amazing.

2538
01:39:17,546 --> 01:39:18,546
(Plump and appetizing)

2539
01:39:19,686 --> 01:39:21,526
It doesn't smell bad at all. It's fascinating.

2540
01:39:21,956 --> 01:39:23,426
Seeing it flattened like this...

2541
01:39:23,826 --> 01:39:25,546
- It's incredible.
- The folded one is one.

2542
01:39:26,126 --> 01:39:28,796
(If you spread the wild eel inside the bag, )

2543
01:39:30,026 --> 01:39:33,236
(it fills the entire gridiron.)

2544
01:39:33,366 --> 01:39:35,136
- This is really amazing.
- Right.

2545
01:39:36,866 --> 01:39:38,906
(Everyone is enjoying the wonderful wild eels.)

2546
01:39:39,436 --> 01:39:43,975
(Putting the thick wild eels on the gridiron...)

2547
01:39:43,976 --> 01:39:46,416
(and placing it over the charcoal fire right away.)

2548
01:39:48,546 --> 01:39:50,186
- Shall we use both sides?
- Yes.

2549
01:39:51,016 --> 01:39:52,216
Here.

2550
01:39:52,756 --> 01:39:55,486
(Placing lots of plump wild eel)

2551
01:39:55,886 --> 01:39:56,886
(Sprinkling salt gently)

2552
01:39:56,887 --> 01:39:59,655
The salt pops because of the fire. Be careful.

2553
01:39:59,656 --> 01:40:01,095
(It's guaranteed to be delicious.)

2554
01:40:01,096 --> 01:40:03,026
You can sprinkle plenty. It'll fall anyway.

2555
01:40:03,466 --> 01:40:06,435
You built a good fire.

2556
01:40:06,436 --> 01:40:07,612
(While a work of art is being made...)

2557
01:40:07,636 --> 01:40:09,806
Next, I will...

2558
01:40:10,906 --> 01:40:12,312
If I start making napa cabbage soup first...

2559
01:40:12,336 --> 01:40:13,805
For napa cabbage soup, I just need to make a broth,

2560
01:40:13,806 --> 01:40:15,276
add napa cabbage and doenjang.

2561
01:40:15,976 --> 01:40:17,676
- Then how...
- Add garlic too.

2562
01:40:18,246 --> 01:40:20,675
I should add seasoning powder bag first.

2563
01:40:20,676 --> 01:40:22,222
(Sun Young is making a soup on her own?)

2564
01:40:22,246 --> 01:40:24,586
(Actually, Sun Young has been...)

2565
01:40:24,886 --> 01:40:25,956
(Jung Ah!)

2566
01:40:26,186 --> 01:40:27,256
(Jung Ah!)

2567
01:40:27,656 --> 01:40:29,626
(Ma'am?)

2568
01:40:29,986 --> 01:40:33,896
(She's only assisted Captain Yum for the main dish.)

2569
01:40:36,126 --> 01:40:39,196
(She's making a main dish for the first time today.)

2570
01:40:39,536 --> 01:40:41,565
(They're going to have refreshing napa cabbage soup...)

2571
01:40:41,566 --> 01:40:42,606
(with grilled wild eels.)

2572
01:40:43,136 --> 01:40:45,606
Shall we look for the seasoning powder bag together?

2573
01:40:46,236 --> 01:40:47,536
Yes.

2574
01:40:49,076 --> 01:40:50,076
Two.

2575
01:40:50,646 --> 01:40:51,646
Two?

2576
01:40:51,647 --> 01:40:52,967
(Cooking with viewers? Is she...)

2577
01:40:53,146 --> 01:40:56,116
(Kim Sun Young's Best Cooking Secrets)

2578
01:40:56,786 --> 01:41:01,086
(Today's menu, doenjang napa cabbage soup)

2579
01:41:01,586 --> 01:41:03,956
Shall we make it in the pretty green pot?

2580
01:41:05,056 --> 01:41:06,495
A really pretty green pot.

2581
01:41:06,496 --> 01:41:07,926
(She chose a pretty pot.)

2582
01:41:08,326 --> 01:41:09,326
Broth.

2583
01:41:10,066 --> 01:41:12,495
Let's make a broth with the seasoning powder bag.

2584
01:41:12,496 --> 01:41:14,136
(Add a seasoning powder bag and boil it.)

2585
01:41:14,496 --> 01:41:15,866
Isn't the pot too small?

2586
01:41:16,806 --> 01:41:18,665
She told me to make just a little.

2587
01:41:18,666 --> 01:41:21,336
- Just a little...
- But that's way too small.

2588
01:41:22,076 --> 01:41:24,706
(Returning to Fresh off the Sea with generous Captain Yum)

2589
01:41:25,046 --> 01:41:27,146
- This is small?
- Yes, we have that much cabbage.

2590
01:41:27,876 --> 01:41:29,015
There's quite a lot.

2591
01:41:29,016 --> 01:41:30,586
(Piled)

2592
01:41:31,316 --> 01:41:33,115
(Ms. Kim Sun Young has hit a roadblock as soon as she started.)

2593
01:41:33,116 --> 01:41:34,116
This is small?

2594
01:41:35,926 --> 01:41:37,046
We're making more than this?

2595
01:41:37,626 --> 01:41:39,126
All right. I got it.

2596
01:41:40,096 --> 01:41:41,416
Shall we make it in a bigger pot?

2597
01:41:43,526 --> 01:41:47,036
(Today's menu, doenjang napa cabbage soup in a large quantity)

2598
01:41:49,136 --> 01:41:51,036
(Making a mistake right away)

2599
01:41:51,906 --> 01:41:54,476
(Making a fuss)

2600
01:41:55,276 --> 01:41:58,246
(It's not easy to make a main dish for the first time.)

2601
01:41:58,776 --> 01:41:59,846
This big?

2602
01:42:02,486 --> 01:42:05,016
(Added 2L of water as it's in a large quantity)

2603
01:42:11,056 --> 01:42:12,386
The fire isn't on.

2604
01:42:13,226 --> 01:42:15,696
(Even the fire is off too?)

2605
01:42:16,126 --> 01:42:18,125
- The fire isn't on.
- The fire isn't on.

2606
01:42:18,126 --> 01:42:19,196
The fire isn't on?

2607
01:42:20,896 --> 01:42:24,666
(Infusing the seasoning bag in cold water)

2608
01:42:25,436 --> 01:42:26,436
That's a lot of water.

2609
01:42:27,806 --> 01:42:29,806
I can boil it with the lid open. It'll boil down.

2610
01:42:31,506 --> 01:42:33,546
(Gulping)

2611
01:42:33,776 --> 01:42:35,845
Jung Ah! Are anchovy broth...

2612
01:42:35,846 --> 01:42:37,586
and anchovy sauce different?

2613
01:42:37,786 --> 01:42:39,286
Yes, they're totally different.

2614
01:42:39,816 --> 01:42:42,486
- Don't bring anchovy broth.
- Okay.

2615
01:42:43,726 --> 01:42:44,926
Anchovy sauce...

2616
01:42:45,686 --> 01:42:47,556
Premium anchovy... Sand lance sauce?

2617
01:42:50,026 --> 01:42:51,065
Where is the anchovy sauce?

2618
01:42:51,066 --> 01:42:54,436
(Will Sun Young be able to make napa cabbage soup?)

2619
01:42:55,236 --> 01:42:56,365
(Captain Yum is preparing glutinous rice.)

2620
01:42:56,366 --> 01:43:02,436
(Pouring rice)

2621
01:43:03,076 --> 01:43:05,876
(While deciding menus for Eat Together yesterday morning, )

2622
01:43:06,076 --> 01:43:07,245
(Jung Ah thought of yakbab.)

2623
01:43:07,246 --> 01:43:08,416
(Yakbab? That's incredible.)

2624
01:43:08,776 --> 01:43:09,815
(They'll make yakbab for dessert.)

2625
01:43:09,816 --> 01:43:10,936
(I'm good at making yakbab.)

2626
01:43:11,346 --> 01:43:15,316
(As it takes a long time, she'll make it a day before.)

2627
01:43:15,716 --> 01:43:18,556
(Yoon Seo was highly looking for it too.)

2628
01:43:19,226 --> 01:43:21,825
(Jung Ah starts making yakbab...)

2629
01:43:21,826 --> 01:43:23,065
(in bulk.)

2630
01:43:23,066 --> 01:43:25,596
(Emptying it out)

2631
01:43:26,236 --> 01:43:29,065
(It's more than just a huge batch of yakbab.)

2632
01:43:29,066 --> 01:43:31,666
(It's 40 servings of yakbab.)

2633
01:43:32,206 --> 01:43:34,526
(Even Captain Yum hasn't made this much yakbab in one go.)

2634
01:43:34,706 --> 01:43:37,046
(The biggest batch of yakbab you've ever seen)

2635
01:43:37,606 --> 01:43:39,646
(40 servings of glutinous rice)

2636
01:43:40,416 --> 01:43:42,546
(Over 30 jujubes)

2637
01:43:42,716 --> 01:43:45,116
- We don't need to rinse pine nuts.
- And the pumpkin seeds.

2638
01:43:45,216 --> 01:43:47,015
(Two bags of pumpkin seeds)

2639
01:43:47,016 --> 01:43:48,116
This is a lot.

2640
01:43:48,716 --> 01:43:50,456
Well, this is enough for 40 people.

2641
01:43:51,056 --> 01:43:52,496
More ingredients mean deeper flavor.

2642
01:43:53,096 --> 01:43:55,125
I'll cut these and give them a light rinse.

2643
01:43:55,126 --> 01:43:56,566
(Adding over 70 chestnuts)

2644
01:43:56,966 --> 01:43:59,406
(A crazy amount of ingredients for the biggest batch of food)

2645
01:43:59,736 --> 01:44:03,306
(Will she be able to manage this like the generous cook she is?)

2646
01:44:04,206 --> 01:44:06,706
(Slicing them finely to make it easier for elders to eat)

2647
01:44:07,636 --> 01:44:08,676
(Slicing 1 jujube)

2648
01:44:11,346 --> 01:44:14,016
(She slices each one with utmost care.)

2649
01:44:14,776 --> 01:44:17,586
(But there's one problem.)

2650
01:44:18,546 --> 01:44:20,815
(She has to do this over 30 times.)

2651
01:44:20,816 --> 01:44:24,256
(And that's only for jujubes.)

2652
01:44:24,786 --> 01:44:29,795
(She's slicing the jujubes nonstop...)

2653
01:44:29,796 --> 01:44:34,436
(in the same pose.)

2654
01:44:35,266 --> 01:44:37,236
(She's been at this for some time now.)

2655
01:44:37,836 --> 01:44:40,876
(But she still has a pile of jujubes to slice.)

2656
01:44:41,376 --> 01:44:42,436
(Sniffling)

2657
01:44:42,876 --> 01:44:44,006
Oh, my back.

2658
01:44:44,306 --> 01:44:47,016
(She faces the hardship of making 40 servings with jujubes.)

2659
01:44:50,586 --> 01:44:52,885
Hold on. Why is my neck so sore?

2660
01:44:52,886 --> 01:44:54,085
- Your neck is sore?
- Yes.

2661
01:44:54,086 --> 01:44:55,926
(She ends up with a cervical disc herniation.)

2662
01:44:56,486 --> 01:44:58,856
(Is she finally done?)

2663
01:44:59,726 --> 01:45:02,666
(As if. She has to slice 40 servings of chestnuts too.)

2664
01:45:04,026 --> 01:45:05,066
My back hurts.

2665
01:45:05,726 --> 01:45:07,095
(She's out of it.)

2666
01:45:07,096 --> 01:45:08,836
(Worried)

2667
01:45:09,266 --> 01:45:10,582
We need to cut them into quarters?

2668
01:45:10,606 --> 01:45:12,506
- This... No, not into quarters.
- Okay.

2669
01:45:13,406 --> 01:45:14,505
- I see. Like that.
- This big.

2670
01:45:14,506 --> 01:45:16,282
(No matter how exhausting it is, she cuts them into small pieces.)

2671
01:45:16,306 --> 01:45:17,745
- Should I do this?
- Cut them like this. Yes.

2672
01:45:17,746 --> 01:45:19,315
- Then give them a gentle rinse.
- Sure.

2673
01:45:19,316 --> 01:45:20,815
(They finally switch places.)

2674
01:45:20,816 --> 01:45:22,786
These chestnuts will taste great in yakbab.

2675
01:45:24,486 --> 01:45:26,816
(Let me get started now.)

2676
01:45:27,586 --> 01:45:30,125
(Yoon Seo, the art major, )

2677
01:45:30,126 --> 01:45:32,756
(neatly slices the chestnuts.)

2678
01:45:33,656 --> 01:45:35,702
(Meanwhile, Sun Young's broth has developed a rich flavor.)

2679
01:45:35,726 --> 01:45:36,865
I'll add the napa cabbages.

2680
01:45:36,866 --> 01:45:38,772
(She adds the napa cabbages to the doenjang broth.)

2681
01:45:38,796 --> 01:45:40,895
(She grabs a handful of the cabbages...)

2682
01:45:40,896 --> 01:45:42,396
(and adds them to the broth.)

2683
01:45:44,006 --> 01:45:46,376
(She's adding another handful?)

2684
01:45:48,006 --> 01:45:50,746
(A pile of napa cabbages)

2685
01:45:51,346 --> 01:45:52,476
This is too much.

2686
01:45:54,746 --> 01:45:55,815
It's too much.

2687
01:45:55,816 --> 01:45:57,322
(She's a generous cook just like Jung Ah.)

2688
01:45:57,346 --> 01:45:59,185
It's more than I thought.

2689
01:45:59,186 --> 01:46:00,732
(But more ingredients mean richer flavor.)

2690
01:46:00,756 --> 01:46:05,386
(How will her generous napa cabbage soup turn out?)

2691
01:46:05,986 --> 01:46:07,456
- Here's a fan.
- Great.

2692
01:46:08,796 --> 01:46:10,695
Fan it gently like this.

2693
01:46:10,696 --> 01:46:12,416
(We need a good wind for this masterpiece.)

2694
01:46:12,736 --> 01:46:16,666
(The wild eels are getting grilled nicely over charcoal.)

2695
01:46:17,206 --> 01:46:20,435
Have you ever seen a Japanese master grill eel?

2696
01:46:20,436 --> 01:46:23,076
- They fan the fire all day.
- This is how they look at the eel.

2697
01:46:23,176 --> 01:46:24,806
- Seriously.
- Like this. I'm serious.

2698
01:46:26,076 --> 01:46:28,616
The way they handle the fan is different.

2699
01:46:28,776 --> 01:46:30,686
- Yes, that's it.
- Right.

2700
01:46:30,886 --> 01:46:32,315
(He suddenly starts dancing with the fan.)

2701
01:46:32,316 --> 01:46:33,886
That's how they snapped their wrist.

2702
01:46:34,516 --> 01:46:35,555
The masterful wrist snap.

2703
01:46:35,556 --> 01:46:38,986
(This is the wrist snap of an eel master.)

2704
01:46:39,496 --> 01:46:40,926
Eels.

2705
01:46:41,596 --> 01:46:43,026
(Laughing)

2706
01:46:43,366 --> 01:46:45,995
It's like he's done this before. He looks like a real eel master.

2707
01:46:45,996 --> 01:46:47,836
(Channeling his inner eel master way too hard)

2708
01:46:48,736 --> 01:46:52,066
(He fans the fire and grills one side like a master.)

2709
01:46:52,506 --> 01:46:53,536
Now.

2710
01:46:53,736 --> 01:46:54,736
(Groaning)

2711
01:46:55,876 --> 01:46:57,206
(He confidently flips it over.)

2712
01:46:57,606 --> 01:46:59,305
(How does it look?)

2713
01:46:59,306 --> 01:47:00,345
It's not cooked at all.

2714
01:47:00,346 --> 01:47:02,306
- We should give it more time.
- It's not cooked.

2715
01:47:02,886 --> 01:47:04,345
It's white now. Right?

2716
01:47:04,346 --> 01:47:05,415
(The flesh of the wild eel is still milky white.)

2717
01:47:05,416 --> 01:47:07,756
(He quickly flips it back.)

2718
01:47:08,486 --> 01:47:09,486
(Meowing)

2719
01:47:10,686 --> 01:47:11,885
Oh, my.

2720
01:47:11,886 --> 01:47:13,156
(It still looks tasty.)

2721
01:47:13,356 --> 01:47:15,296
Does it smell good?

2722
01:47:16,796 --> 01:47:17,995
So cute.

2723
01:47:17,996 --> 01:47:20,296
(Dashing over)

2724
01:47:20,496 --> 01:47:22,906
The neighborhood cats are going wild.

2725
01:47:23,806 --> 01:47:25,505
These eels are going to drive them nuts.

2726
01:47:25,506 --> 01:47:27,306
(As the wild eels sizzle to a golden brown, )

2727
01:47:27,836 --> 01:47:30,576
(the neighborhood cats start gathering.)

2728
01:47:30,906 --> 01:47:31,976
(Meowing)

2729
01:47:32,346 --> 01:47:34,576
- Oh, no. They want some.
- They want food.

2730
01:47:34,776 --> 01:47:36,576
Look at that one. It's sitting down politely.

2731
01:47:37,586 --> 01:47:38,885
They're talking to each other.

2732
01:47:38,886 --> 01:47:40,716
(Please give us one eel.)

2733
01:47:40,886 --> 01:47:42,885
But we can't give you our eels.

2734
01:47:42,886 --> 01:47:44,156
We have to eat them.

2735
01:47:44,526 --> 01:47:46,196
I'm sorry. We can't give you eels.

2736
01:47:47,596 --> 01:47:49,965
(Because we worked so hard to catch them.)

2737
01:47:49,966 --> 01:47:52,026
(Precious)

2738
01:47:52,566 --> 01:47:54,135
(He flips the grill net.)

2739
01:47:54,136 --> 01:47:56,166
(Amazed)

2740
01:47:56,406 --> 01:47:57,706
My gosh.

2741
01:47:57,966 --> 01:47:59,476
Yours looks golden brown too.

2742
01:47:59,736 --> 01:48:00,936
(Proud)

2743
01:48:01,336 --> 01:48:02,375
(Cheerfully humming)

2744
01:48:02,376 --> 01:48:04,476
(Golden brown)

2745
01:48:04,946 --> 01:48:06,845
- This side looks better.
- Yes. It's grilled nicely.

2746
01:48:06,846 --> 01:48:07,876
(Appetizing)

2747
01:48:19,656 --> 01:48:20,726
Look at the meat.

2748
01:48:21,596 --> 01:48:24,896
(They can't help but marvel at the fatty meat.)

2749
01:48:25,296 --> 01:48:26,296
(Drawn to the eels by the smell)

2750
01:48:26,297 --> 01:48:27,535
This is a lot of work.

2751
01:48:27,536 --> 01:48:29,366
- This looks amazing.
- It does.

2752
01:48:29,766 --> 01:48:30,766
I want to look too.

2753
01:48:31,766 --> 01:48:32,876
(Amazed)

2754
01:48:34,306 --> 01:48:35,706
(Jaw-dropping)

2755
01:48:36,076 --> 01:48:37,206
Look how thick it is.

2756
01:48:38,076 --> 01:48:39,106
Awesome.

2757
01:48:40,476 --> 01:48:43,216
(Thick)

2758
01:48:45,486 --> 01:48:46,486
This looks so good.

2759
01:48:47,856 --> 01:48:49,316
Gosh, this is no joke.

2760
01:48:49,956 --> 01:48:51,185
- Look how thick that is.
- This looks so good.

2761
01:48:51,186 --> 01:48:52,725
(Masterpiece)

2762
01:48:52,726 --> 01:48:54,046
- This is...
- It smells amazing.

2763
01:48:55,592 --> 01:48:58,521
(Their third labor, green plum)

2764
01:48:58,522 --> 01:48:59,892
(Only three of them will go.)

2765
01:49:00,462 --> 01:49:01,891
(The one going home...)

2766
01:49:01,892 --> 01:49:03,708
(versus the ones going to the green plum field)

2767
01:49:03,732 --> 01:49:05,372
(A mind game with their fate on the line)

2768
01:49:05,432 --> 01:49:07,032
(A sip can result in death.)

2769
01:49:07,272 --> 01:49:08,801
(Only the one with the right pick...)

2770
01:49:08,802 --> 01:49:10,602
(can smile.)

2771
01:49:11,342 --> 01:49:16,012
(Which three will go work on the green plum field tomorrow?)

2772
01:49:19,582 --> 01:49:22,181
(A voice resonates throughout the village in Hadong.)

2773
01:49:22,182 --> 01:49:24,051
(Is that Jung Ah's voice?)

2774
01:49:24,052 --> 01:49:27,322
(Serving 40 residents of the village)

2775
01:49:27,552 --> 01:49:30,561
(A project for Jung Ah to level up from generous to bountiful)

2776
01:49:30,562 --> 01:49:32,121
(They're running out of time.)

2777
01:49:32,122 --> 01:49:33,731
(They're short-handed too.)

2778
01:49:33,732 --> 01:49:36,061
(They're lacking willpower as well.)

2779
01:49:36,062 --> 01:49:38,461
(Jung Ah is about to lose it.)

2780
01:49:38,462 --> 01:49:40,532
(There's no time to waste now.)

2781
01:49:40,632 --> 01:49:41,701
(Remaining time)

2782
01:49:41,702 --> 01:49:43,172
(Only 5 minutes)

